<% page_title t("legal.terms.title") %>
<% page_meta t("legal.edition", date: l(Legal::VERSION.to_date, format: :long)) %>

<article class="legal">
  <p class="muted">This is a translation for convenience; for users in Russia the Russian version prevails.</p>

  <p>This is an agreement between you and <%= operator(:name) %> ("we") about using the Heartwood service. By signing up you accept it.</p>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>Heartwood is a service for keeping a family tree together. Its source code is open under AGPL-3.0; these terms cover our hosted service.</p>

  <h2>2. Your data stays yours</h2>
  <p>Everything you put into a tree belongs to you. We get no rights to it beyond what is needed to store it and show it to you and your tree's members. You can download your tree as standard GEDCOM and delete your account at any time.</p>

  <h2>3. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>use the service from the age of 14; younger children only together with a parent;</li>
    <li>enter information about other people only for personal and family purposes, and respect their rights. Enter living people with their knowledge, and remove them if they object;</li>
    <li>don't enter the health, religion or ethnicity of living people;</li>
    <li>don't upload material you have no rights to, or that the law forbids;</li>
    <li>keep your password secret and invite only people you trust: an invited editor can change the tree.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Plans</h2>
  <p>The basics are free, with a limit on people per tree. A paid plan removes the limits; payment terms are published separately. When a paid plan ends, your data is never locked or deleted.</p>

  <h2>5. Liability</h2>
  <p>We are liable to you as the law provides and do everything reasonable to keep your data safe, including change history and backups. The free plan comes with no uptime guarantee; the paid plan's terms are in the offer. We recommend downloading a copy of your tree from time to time.</p>

  <h2>6. Ending</h2>
  <p>You can stop at any time by deleting your account. We may restrict access for a serious breach of these terms, first letting you download your data unless the law forbids it.</p>

  <h2>7. If material infringes your rights</h2>
  <p>If a photo or other material in a tree infringes your copyright or other rights, write to <%= operator(:email) %>: what the material is, which tree it is in and why it infringes. We consider such notices within 10 working days and remove the material if the claim is justified (Civil Code of the RF, art. 1253.1).</p>

  <h2>8. Other</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by Russian law. We email you about changes at least 10 days in advance. Changes never worsen the terms of a period already paid for; if you disagree, you can delete your account and get the money for a paid period back under the offer. Questions: <%= operator(:email) %>.</p>
</article>
